# Open Higgsfield AI — environment variables
#
# The Next.js studio (npm run dev / npm run build) does not read any of these.
# Leave this file as documentation. Do not put real secrets in it, and do not
# commit a filled-in .env.
#
# Generation API key (required to generate, not required to boot the UI)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no MUAPI_API_KEY / KIE_API_KEY build variable for the studio.
# On first visit the UI asks for a key and stores it in the browser under
# localStorage key `kie_key`. The studio then calls https://api.kie.ai from
# the browser with `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
#
# That key is client-side by design. Do not set it as NEXT_PUBLIC_* or VITE_*:
# those prefixes are inlined into the JavaScript bundle and would publish the
# secret to every visitor.
#
# This fork sends the key to kie.ai, not muapi.ai. A muapi.ai key will not
# authenticate. Create a key at https://kie.ai/api-key
#
# Content-factory / MATAI backend (Netlify functions only)
# --------------------------------------------------------
# `npm run vite:dev` serves the MATAI client. It stays on the sign-in screen
# until /.netlify/functions/session succeeds. Those functions read the
# variables below. They are not required for the Next.js studio on Vercel.
# Set them in the host dashboard (Netlify or Vercel), never in git.

# Required for MATAI sign-in and library
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# COMPOSIO_ORG_ID=
# COMPOSIO_PROJECT_ID=
# AUTOM8_AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=
# MATAI_SESSION_SECRET=

# Accepted aliases / optional integrations
# AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=
# AIRTABLE_AUTH=
# AIRTABLE_API_KEY=
# AIRTABLE_TOKEN=
# AIRTABLE_PAT=
# CHAMPION_AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=
# KIE_API_KEY=
# KIE_AI_API_KEY=
# FAL_KEY=
# FAL_API_KEY=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# RESEND_FROM=
# NOTIFY_EMAIL=
# ADMIN_EMAIL=
# OWNER_EMAIL=
# ACCESS_CODE=
